---
layout: layouts/feature.njk
wide: true
title: "Apps and navigation | Shellui"
description: "Run apps built in React, Vue, Svelte, Angular, or plain HTML inside one Shellui shell. Share navigation, layout, theme, language, and dialogs."
eyebrow: Features
eleventyComputed:
  heading: "{{ mfeIntro.heading }}"
  lede: "{{ mfeIntro.lede }}"
---

{% include "framework-icons.njk" %}
{% include "mfe-intro.njk" %}

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="any-stack">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="any-stack" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Built with shadcn/ui, open to any stack</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">The Shellui interface uses shadcn/ui and Tailwind CSS. Your apps do not have to. The shell shares its theme as CSS variables with the shadcn/ui names, and the SDK applies them to your app, light or dark.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">When people switch theme in the shell, every app follows. Pick the path that matches your app.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10 grid max-w-4xl gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6"><p class="text-sm font-semibold text-foreground">Already on shadcn/ui</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Same token names. Your components match the shell with no mapping.</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6"><p class="text-sm font-semibold text-foreground">Tailwind CSS</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Point your theme colors at the shell variables and your utilities follow every theme switch.</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6"><p class="text-sm font-semibold text-foreground">Any other stack</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Vue, Svelte, Angular, or plain CSS. Read the same variables wherever you want the shell colors.</p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Starters for React, Vue, Svelte, Angular, Next.js, Nuxt, Alpine.js, and Tauri come connected. The <a class="font-medium text-primary-ink underline underline-offset-2" href="{{ site.docs }}/features/themes/">themes guide</a> shows the code.</p>
</section>

{# Future screenshot: Playground shell with iframe app. Add a real image here when available. #}

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="layout-modes">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="layout-modes" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Choose a layout for your product</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Pick one layout for the whole product and every app inherits it. Try them below to see the shell rearrange around your app.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Apps that fill their iframe follow every layout. <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">windows</code> is a proof of concept and not ready for production.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10">
    {% include "shell-layouts-playground.njk" %}
  </div>
</section>
<script src="/assets/js/shell-layouts.js" type="module"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/anim-card.js" type="module"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/hero-dots.js" type="module"></script>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="components">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="components" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Shared components, drawn by the shell</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Toasts, dialogs, modals, and drawers open from any app with one SDK call. Shellui draws them in the shell, outside the iframe, so they cover the full window and look the same in every app. Hover or focus a card to play it.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
    {% for c in uiComponents %}
      {% set wide = loop.last and loop.length % 2 %}
      <article id="component-{{ c.id }}" tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="component-{{ c.id }}-title" class="anim-card flex min-w-0{% if wide %} md:col-span-2 md:flex-row{% endif %} flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border bg-card focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary">
        <div class="p-6{% if wide %} md:flex md:w-2/5 md:flex-col md:justify-center{% endif %}">
          <h3 id="component-{{ c.id }}-title" class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground">{{ c.title }}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">{{ c.line }}</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Call <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">{{ c.call }}</code> {{ c.how }}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="anim-visual relative mt-auto border-t border-border bg-muted{% if wide %} md:mt-0 md:w-3/5 md:border-t-0 md:border-l{% endif %}" data-anim-play>
          {% include c.visual %}
          <button type="button" class="anim-play" aria-label="Play {{ c.title | lower }} animation">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" aria-hidden="true"><circle class="anim-ring" cx="20" cy="20" r="19"/><circle class="anim-ring-fill" cx="20" cy="20" r="19" pathLength="100"/><path class="anim-icon" d="M16 13.5v13l10.5-6.5z"/></svg>
          </button>
        </div>
      </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section id="theming" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="theming-heading">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="theming-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Your brand, their language, every app</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Pick a theme and a language in the shell. Every shadcn/ui component in every app follows with the same colors, corners, and words.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10">
    {% include "feature-visual-theme-language.njk" %}
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="mt-16 max-w-3xl border-0 border-t border-border">
<div class="mt-10">{% set playgroundCtaWide = true %}{% include "playground-cta.njk" %}</div>

